    },
    {
      "name": "History year and month disclosures",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "history-year-header",
      "description": "History-only native disclosure hierarchy. Values are illustrative; disclosure state is native and the real page preserves it across rendering.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-year\" open><summary><h2>Tax year 2026</h2><span class=\"ds-stats\"><span><strong>$125.50</strong><small>Deduction</small></span><span><strong>12</strong><small>Receipts</small></span><span><strong>28</strong><small>GF items</small></span></span></summary><div class=\"ds-year-content\"><details class=\"ds-month\" open><summary><h3>October</h3><span class=\"ds-stats\"><span><strong>$25.50</strong><small>Deduction</small></span><span><strong>3</strong><small>Receipts</small></span><span><strong>6</strong><small>GF items</small></span></span></summary><p class=\"ds-month-content\">Receipt rows use the shared workspace layout.</p></details></div></details>",
      "css": ".ds-year,.ds-month{font-family:var(--font-body,Inter,sans-serif);color:var(--text,#1F2937);border:0;background:transparent}.ds-year>summary,.ds-month>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;min-height:84px;padding:20px 24px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;border-radius:12px;transition:background .2s}.ds-year>summary{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--primary,#22C55E) 6%,var(--bg,#F8FAF8))}.ds-year>summary:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--primary,#22C55E) 10%,var(--bg,#F8FAF8))}.ds-year>summary::-webkit-details-marker,.ds-month>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-year>summary::before,.ds-month>summary::before{content:\"\";flex:0 0 8px;width:8px;height:8px;border-right:1.5px solid var(--workspace-muted,#59665F);border-bottom:1.5px solid var(--workspace-muted,#59665F);transform:rotate(-45deg);transition:transform .2s var(--ease-out,cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1))}.ds-year[open]>summary::before,.ds-month[open]>summary::before{transform:rotate(45deg)}.ds-year>summary:focus-visible,.ds-month>summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary-hover,#16A34A);outline-offset:3px}.ds-year h2,.ds-month h3{margin:0;font-family:var(--font-display,Manrope,Inter,sans-serif);font-size:18px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;white-space:nowrap}.ds-stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(110px,1.2fr) repeat(2,minmax(72px,1fr));gap:28px;margin-left:auto;text-align:right;align-items:baseline}.ds-stats>span{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}.ds-stats strong{font-family:var(--font-metrics,Manrope,Inter,sans-serif);font-variant-numeric:lining-nums tabular-nums;font-size:18px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.2}.ds-stats>span:first-child strong{font-size:26px;font-weight:600}.ds-stats small{font-size:12px;color:var(--workspace-muted,#59665F)}.ds-year-content{padding:12px 20px 0}.ds-month>summary{min-height:80px;padding:16px 12px}.ds-month>summary:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--primary,#22C55E) 4%,var(--bg,#F8FAF8))}.ds-month h3,.ds-month .ds-stats strong{font-size:16px}.ds-month .ds-stats>span:first-child strong{font-size:20px;font-weight:600}.ds-month-content{padding:12px;color:var(--text-secondary,#6B7280);font-size:13px}@media(max-width:700px){.ds-year>summary,.ds-month>summary{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;padding:18px 16px}.ds-stats{flex-basis:100%;margin-left:24px;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;text-align:left}.ds-stats strong{font-size:16px}.ds-stats>span:first-child strong{font-size:24px}.ds-year-content{padding:8px 0 0 8px}.ds-month>summary{padding:16px 8px}.ds-month .ds-stats>span:first-child strong{font-size:20px}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-year>summary,.ds-month>summary,.ds-year>summary::before,.ds-month>summary::before{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "History mobile scan action",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "On History at mobile widths (860px and below), the existing scan action docks wholly inside the bottom-navigation footprint, leaving receipt delete controls unobscured. History navigation reserves a fourth visual slot with right padding (70px). The existing fixed scan wrapper sits at bottom calc(19px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px)), right max(23px, calc((100vw - 340px) / 2 + 7px)), with stacking level (96). Its scan button is (54px square), has no shadow, and hides its main label; camera/upload options retain readable labels and a minimum width (180px). This is a History-only placement rule. The same open-year/open-month review condition still hides both scan and bottom navigation. The isolated native-disclosure preview below illustrates button and option styling; production retains its existing scan-menu behavior.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-scan\"><summary aria-label=\"Scan a receipt\"><svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"ds-scan-options\"><button type=\"button\">Take a picture</button><button type=\"button\">Upload a photo</button></div></details>",
      "css": ".ds-scan{display:inline-block;position:relative;font-family:var(--font-body,Inter,sans-serif)}.ds-scan>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:54px;height:54px;padding:0;border:0;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;cursor:pointer;background:var(--primary,#22C55E);color:#fff;box-shadow:none;transition:background .2s,transform .2s}.ds-scan>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-scan>summary:hover{background:var(--primary-hover,#16A34A)}.ds-scan>summary:focus-visible,.ds-scan-options button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--primary,#22C55E);outline-offset:3px}.ds-scan>summary:active{transform:scale(.97)}.ds-scan-options{display:grid;gap:8px;margin-top:12px}.ds-scan-options button{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:180px;min-height:44px;padding:0 16px;border:1px solid var(--border,#E5E7EB);border-radius:999px;background:var(--card,#fff);color:var(--text,#1F2937);font-family:var(--font-body,Inter,sans-serif);font-size:13px;cursor:pointer}.ds-scan-options button:hover{background:var(--accent-light,#DCFCE7)}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-scan>summary{transition:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A calm green workspace",
    "overview": "BreadWinner's incumbent identity combines fresh green, green-tinted backgrounds, softly rounded controls, and Inter with Manrope. Preserve the existing logo, top navigation, theme support, and shared interaction language. The descriptive north star records the implementation rather than inventing product positioning.\n\nThe Home and History extension makes receipt work sleek, elegant, compact, and direct, with less repeated copy and visible editing actions. The pastel-consumer direction (seed 2024013947) is translated into the existing palette and navigation. Home retains its own gradient metrics platform; Home and History now share the receipt row, toolbar, editor, and photo-dialog language. History preserves its calendar-year and month disclosure groups. These scoped extensions are not a sitewide restyle mandate. Camera styling is inherited and remains a distinct treatment; this document does not authorize broader drift repair.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Existing green identity and theme-aware surfaces.",
      "One dominant Home amount above three supporting metrics.",
      "Shared Home and History receipt rows with visible review and price editing.",
      "Native History year/month groups with clear deduction hierarchy.",
      "Responsive editing with explicit comparison approval."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Approval Rule",
        "body": "A suggested comparison stays visually distinct from an approved amount. Its deduction does not count until the user approves it.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the existing green palette, Inter/Manrope, logo, navigation, and themes.",
      "Do keep the Home deduction dominant, with three supporting metrics below on a compact gradient platform.",
      "Do make prices, deletion, comparison, and review visibly actionable and keyboard reachable.",
      "Do count only approved comparisons.",
      "Do retain labeled fields, responsive photo placement, reduced motion, and the mobile review exit.",
      "Do preserve native History year/month disclosures, calendar-year grouping, open-state persistence, filters, and exports."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't turn the Home composition into a sitewide restyle requirement.",
      "Don't repeat the same explanation across the greeting, summary, and receipt workspace.",
      "Don't replace explicit review and price editing with unlabeled icon-only discovery.",
      "Don't redesign inherited camera styling as part of these receipt workspace extensions."
    ]
  }
}
